{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Before the Adon.</b> Who arranges your affairs in natural things, as in וְלַאָדוֹן לְכָל בֵּיתוֹ (Genesis 45:8)." "<b>Elohei Israel.</b> Who arranges Israel's affairs in spiritual matters, which are above nature, which would not befit any but the separate intelligences called Elohim, as in זֹבֵחַ לָאֱלֹהִים יָחֳרָם (Exodus 22:19), and as in אֱלָהִין דִּי מְדֹרְהוֹן עִם בִּשְׂרָא לָא אִיתוֹהִי (Daniel 2:11). Therefore He said of the demons לֹא אֱלוֹהַּ (Deuteronomy 32:17), because they possess matter and die like human beings, as the Sages of blessed memory noted (Ḥagigah 16a). And expert judges are also called Elohim, for they sometimes judge without the senses, as with Solomon, of whom it says כִּי חָכְמַת אֱלֹהִים בְּקִרְבּוֹ לַעֲשׂוֹת מִשְׁפָּט (1 Kings 3:28), and as it says וְלֹא לְמַרְאֵה עֵינָיו יִשְׁפּוֹט, וְלֹא לְמִשְׁמַע אָזְנָיו יוֹכִיחַ (Isaiah 11:3). Therefore the blessed El is called אֱלֹהֵי הָאֱלֹהִים (Deuteronomy 10:17) — Who arranges the affairs of the arrangers of supra-natural things, namely the intelligences separate from matter — and אֲדוֹנֵי הָאֲדוֹנִים (Deuteronomy 10:17) — Who arranges the affairs of the arrangers of natural things, namely the celestial bodies. He said, then, יֵרָאֶה כָּל זְכוּרְךָ — to give thanks for the good drawn from Him to you in natural things, inasmuch as He is Israel's Adon, and for that drawn from Him unto eternal life, inasmuch as He is Israel's Elohim."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:15.179752797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}